docker-compose.yml
# The dev interpreter pin must not enter the image. `.python-version` requests an EXACT
# patch (3.12.13), the builder runs `FROM python:3.12-slim` with UV_PYTHON_DOWNLOADS=never,
# and the base image moves to a new 3.12 patch on its own schedule. When it does, `uv sync`
# fails with "No interpreter found for Python 3.12.13" and is not permitted to download one,
# so the image build breaks with no commit having touched it - which is exactly how the
# `docker` job went red on main while every other gate stayed green.
#
# Ignoring it here is the fix rather than pinning the base image to the patch, because
# UV_PYTHON_DOWNLOADS=never already states the intent: use the interpreter the image ships.
# `requires-python = ">=3.12"` is the constraint that actually matters for the build, and the
# exact pin stays in place for local development where reproducibility is the point.
.python-version
tests/
PREVIOUS.md
*.md
